{{Quote|What caused this damage?"<br />"A Mudhorn."<br />"Then you have earned the Mudhorn as your signet.|"[[The Armorer]]" and [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref>}}
'''Mudhorns''' were large horned creatures that inhabited [[Arvala-7]]. The [[Mudhorn egg|eggs]] of mudhorns were considered a delicacy by [[Jawa]]s.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Mudhorn-TMH.png|thumb|left|250px|The mudhorn was covered in wooly fur often coated in mud.]]
Mudhorns had a large horn, flat [[Tooth|teeth]], and long, wooly [[Hair|fur]]. It was oviparous, laying a single [[Mudhorn egg|egg]] per clutch. The egg was huge and was cherished by Jawas. The exterior of this [[egg]] was woolly in the same manner as the skin of the mudhorn, and the interior yolk was [[Color|yellow]].<ref name="Chapter 2" />

==History==
In [[231 BBY]],<ref name="Date note">The events of ''[[The High Republic: Race to Crashpoint Tower]]'' take place concurrently to ''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]'' which take in [[231 BBY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> a mudhorn was in captivity at the [[Lonisa City Zoo]]. During the [[Nihil]]'s [[Valo Atrocity|attack]] on the [[Republic Fair]] taking place in the city, the animals in the [[zoo]] broke free. The zoo's mudhorn soon charged [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]]s [[Ram Jomaram]] and [[Lula Mrala-Talisola|Lula Talisola]], but Talisola used [[the Force]] to trip the animal. The mudhorn crashed sideways into the ground and slid into a storefront, causing it to shatter. The creature then stood and lumbered away.<ref name="Race to Crashpoint Tower">''[[The High Republic: Race to Crashpoint Tower]]''</ref>

[[File:Mudhorn-TMS01E02.png|thumb|right|250px|A mudhorn prepares to charge Din Djarin.]]
Around [[9 ABY]], a mudhorn encountered and fought [[Din Djarin]], a [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]], as the latter attempted to retrieve an egg from the mudhorn's [[Mudhorn cave|cave]]. It was ultimately killed with the help of the [[Force-sensitive]] child, [[Din Grogu|Grogu]].<ref name="Chapter 2" /> The mudhorn later became the [[signet]] of the new Mandalorian [[Clan Mudhorn|clan]] that was founded with Djarin and Grogu.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The mudhorn first appeared in [[Chapter 2: The Child|Chapter 2]] of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', directed by [[Rick Famuyiwa]],<ref name="Chapter 2" /> which aired on [[November 15]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref>

